    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG Estate Agents are delighted to present No. 40 Hampton Wood, an attractive and spacious three bedroom duplex property ideally located in this highly sought after development.\n\nPresented in excellent condition throughout, this well proportioned home extends to approximately 88.7 sq. m. (955 sq. ft.) and offers bright, comfortable accommodation over two floors.\n\nThe ground floor comprises a welcoming entrance hallway, fully fitted kitchen/dining area, generous living room and convenient guest wc. Upstairs, there are three well sized bedrooms, with the principal bedroom benefiting from an ensuite and access to a private balcony, along with a family bathroom.\n\nThe property further benefits from gas fired central heating, UPVC double glazed windows and a designated parking space to the rear.\n\nHampton Wood is ideally positioned with excellent public transport links providing easy access to Dublin City Centre. A selection of local schools, including St. Canice's, St. Kevin's, St. Joseph's and Coláiste Íde, are all within easy reach. Finglas Village and Charlestown Shopping Centre are also within walking distance, while Dublin Airport, the M50 and DCU are all just a short drive away.\n\nNo. 40 will appeal to a wide range of purchasers, including first-time buyers and investors seeking a well presented property in a convenient and established Dublin 11 location.\n\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate what this property has to offer.\n\nLocal DNG Agents: Isabel O'Neill, Ciaran Jones, Vincent Mullen, Michelle Keeley, Leah Barry & Brian McGee MIPAV."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntance Hall - 6.30m x 3.74m\nSmart entrance hallway with laminate wood flooring and painted decor.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - 4.65m x 2.53m\nSituated to the front of the property. Tiled flooring, stylish cream fitted wall and floor units and splashback tiles.\n\nLiving Room - 4.10m x 4.98m\nSituated at the rear of the property, large inviting room with laminate wood flooring, painted decor and feature wall with wallpaper and stove fire. French doors leading to fully decked garden area with carpark access.\n\nDownstairs wc - 1.77m x 1.15m\nLaminate wood flooring, painted decor, wc and whb.\n\nBedroom 1 - 3.83m x 3.68m\nSituated to the front of the property, double room with feature wallpaper and painted decor. Laminate wood flooring throughout and built in wardrobes - access to en suite bathroom and balcony.\n\nEn Suite - 0.74m x 2.31m\nFully tiled upgraded bathroom with whb, wc and shower cubicle.\n\nBalcony - 1.00m x 1.48m\nAccess via Bedroom 1.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.22m x 2.73m\nSituated to the rear of the property. Double room with laminate wood flooring, painted decor and built in wardrobes.\n\nBedroom 3 - 3.22m x 2.10m\nSituated to the rear of the property. Laminate wood flooring, painted decor and built in wardrobes.\n\nBathroom - 2.85m x 1.69m\nFully tiled upgraded bathroom with Jacuzzi bath and over head shower, wc and whb.\n\nRear Garden - \nFully decked garden with carpark access.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Year of construction 2008</li><li> Management Fee 900 per annum</li><li> 1 designated carpark space</li><li> Upgraded bathrooms</li><li> 3 bedrooms/3 bathrooms</li><li> Fully decked rear garden</li><li> Double glazed windows</li><li> Walking distance to Finglas Village, Schools, Café's Bars & Restaurant's</li><li> Surrounded by a host of sports facilities</li><li> Close to City Centre, Dublin Airport, M50 motorway and Charlestown Shopping Centre</ul>"
      },
